explore-design direction library: the taste, minimalist-editorial and
industrial-brutalist directions are adapted from taste-skill by Leon Lin.

Upstream-Repo: https://github.com/Leonxlnx/taste-skill
Upstream-Paths: skills/taste-skill/SKILL.md (taste, commits 3c7017d to 9b7d575);
  minimalist-skill/SKILL.md (added bd7e147); brutalist-skill/SKILL.md (added c826a41)

Local changes: split into explore-design direction references; scope and
approval moved to explore-design's medium-and-providers reference; universal
quality rules moved out to implement's ui-build floor (page-craft.md);
image-generation priority replaced by the owner's imagery choice; invented
client logos replaced by tagged placeholders; the block-library contract
removed and the motion code skeletons split into an on-demand
motion-skeletons.md.


clean-geist direction (references/directions/clean-geist.md): adapted from the
visual system (Part B) of landing-page-design by Elaya.

Upstream-Repo: https://github.com/elayadesign/ai-design-skills
Upstream-Path: skills/landing-page-design
Upstream-Commit: ded7efc9d5c02761c41a03caf3b78f9259ab8828

Local changes: look rules only; craft rules (states, launch checklist,
nested radius, motion safety, content realism) live in implement's
page-craft floor; the advice to invent believable names and figures was
dropped; headline breaks come from max width and text wrapping instead of
manual breaks; the gradient heading is listed as an override of web.md.


liquid-glass direction (references/directions/liquid-glass.md) and the source
register (references/sources.md): rules rewritten in our own words from
Kubai087's "999 tips" posts on X (tips 004 and 010, and the bento card
post), Apple's Human Interface Guidelines (Materials) and the owner's own
glass work. No post text or attached prompt is copied; links and read dates
are in references/sources.md.

Glass code is not included. The direction points to Glasswork by Kubai087
(https://github.com/kubai087/glasswork, MIT), fetched into each project from
its INSTALL.md; projects that ship it keep its MIT notice. Its bundled
wallpapers are Apple's and are not reused.


Background step (references/backgrounds.md) and the galaxy recipe
(references/backgrounds/galaxy/): the owner's own work under this repository's
MIT licence, generalised from the owner's glass-overhaul design round. The
recipe's effects were inspired by amicro by Subhan
(https://github.com/Subhan-code/Amicro--Micro-transitions-, MIT): studied,
nothing copied. The shockwave and the dither/ASCII entry rewrite ideas from
Kubai087's "999 tips" posts on X (tips 013 and 003) in our own words; no post
text or attached prompt is copied. The WebGL wallpaper entry points to
pro-threads by Kubai087 (https://github.com/kubai087/pro-threads, MIT),
fetched into each project, not redistributed.


Structure round (references/coded-mocks.md, G2b), the stuck pick
(references/lavish-review.md, G4) and the content ranking for app screens
(§2b): rules rewritten in our own words from three posts on X by Ian
(ianneo_ai): sorting content before visuals, multi-direction prototypes, and
N versions when stuck. No post text is copied; links and read dates are in
references/sources.md. BoardUI (https://www.boardui.com/) is listed there as
a candidate dashboard kit only; nothing from it is copied.

